.TH UGPIBD 1 "2026-08-01" "ugpibd 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ugpibd \- userspace daemon for USB-GPIB adapters (HiSLIP and Prologix front-ends)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ugpibd
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ugpibd
drives USB-to-GPIB adapters entirely from userspace over
.IR usbfs ,
with no kernel GPIB driver involved, and exposes the attached instruments over
TCP. Two front-ends are available: a HiSLIP server (enabled by default, the
transport pyvisa prefers) and a Prologix-compatible line protocol.
.PP
The Agilent adapters require a firmware upload on every attach.
.B ugpibd
performs this itself from images embedded in the binary; the adapter then
disconnects and re-enumerates under a different USB product id.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " ADDRESS"
Address to bind both servers to. Default
.IR 127.0.0.1 .
Use
.I 0.0.0.0
for all interfaces.
.TP
.BI \-\-hislip\-port " PORT"
TCP port for the HiSLIP server. Default
.IR 4880 .
Set to
.I 0
to disable the HiSLIP front-end.
.TP
.B \-\-enable\-prologix
Enable the Prologix-compatible front-end. Disabled by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
TCP port for the Prologix-compatible server. Default
.IR 1234 .
Only meaningful with
.BR \-\-enable\-prologix .
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " ID"
Adapter backend to use.
.I auto
(the default) detects a single attached adapter by USB VID/PID.
.I list
prints the known backend ids and exits.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List attached supported adapters with their USB port ids, and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-usb\-port " PORT_ID"
Drive the adapter at this USB port id, as reported by
.BR \-\-list .
Required when more than one supported adapter is attached, since
.I auto
detection is ambiguous.
.TP
.BI \-\-default\-address " PAD"
GPIB primary address used when a request does not specify one: the fallback PAD
for HiSLIP clients connecting to a bare
.I hislip0
or
.I gpib0
sub-address, and the initial Prologix
.IR ++addr .
Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout\-ms " MS"
GPIB timeout in milliseconds. Default
.IR 3000 .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase log verbosity.
.B \-v
enables debug logging, which dumps HiSLIP command and response bytes with
non-printables escaped;
.B \-vv
enables trace. Ignored if
.B RUST_LOG
is set.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit. The first line carries the version.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log filter directive, e.g.
.IR ugpibd=debug .
Overrides
.BR \-\-verbose .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/ugpibd
Options for the packaged service. Sets
.B UGPIBD_OPTS
(passed to
.BR ugpibd )
and
.BR UGPIBD_AUTOSTART ,
which opts in to starting the daemon when an adapter is plugged in.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60\-ugpibd.rules
Grants the
.I ugpibd
group access to supported adapters, and triggers
.I ugpibd\-hotplug.service
on attach.
.TP
.I /etc/modprobe.d/ugpibd\-blacklist\-linux\-gpib.conf
Shipped by the optional
.I ugpibd\-blacklist\-linux\-gpib
package. Stops the kernel GPIB drivers claiming these adapters.
.SH STARTING THE DAEMON
The packaged service does not start on its own. Three options:
.TP
.B one-off
.B systemctl start ugpibd
\- works regardless of the autostart setting.
.TP
.B on plug
Set
.B UGPIBD_AUTOSTART=yes
in
.IR /etc/default/ugpibd .
The daemon then starts when a supported adapter appears, and at boot for an
adapter that is already attached.
.TP
.B always
.B systemctl enable ugpibd
\- starts at boot whether or not an adapter is present. The service fails and
gives up if none is found.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.TP
.B failed to claim interface 0
A kernel GPIB driver has claimed the adapter. Install the
.I ugpibd\-blacklist\-linux\-gpib
package, or blacklist
.I agilent_82357a
and
.I ni_usb_gpib
by hand.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/berg/ugpibd/issues \- never to the linux-gpib
project or the kernel
.I drivers/gpib
maintainers, whose drivers this daemon replaces rather than uses.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ugpibd\-scpi (1),
.BR udev (7),
.BR systemd.service (5)
